<header><a href="./" class="brand">CHLOE READS JON / FIELD NOTE</a><a href="./" class="back">← The collection</a></header>
<main><section class="hero"><div class="hero-inner"><div><div class="eyebrow">A pocket-sized experiment in solidarity</div><h1>The <em>Little</em><br>Bridge.</h1><p>Sometimes the distance between “I’m okay” and “I’m not” is a bus ride, a bag of groceries, or fifteen minutes with a screwdriver. Try bridging four ordinary gaps.</p></div><div class="art-frame"><img src="little-bridge-art.png" alt="Paper-cut apartment windows connected by a little bridge of everyday objects" onerror="this.style.display='none';this.nextElementSibling.hidden=false"><svg hidden viewBox="0 0 900 600" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Illustrated glowing footbridge between two neighbourhood windows" style="display:block;width:100%;background:#193742"><rect width="900" height="600" fill="#183642"/><circle cx="710" cy="140" r="92" fill="#efb96e"/><path d="M0 440 175 385 385 480 615 380 900 445V600H0Z" fill="#274d56"/><path d="M0 185h205v415H0zm692 90h208v325H692z" fill="#e19b70"/><path d="M25 230h146v190H25zm695 85h150v175H720z" fill="#f9da9e"/><path d="M58 260h80v122H58zm695 86h81v107h-81z" fill="#294650"/><path d="M197 490Q450 220 704 490l-25 27Q450 294 222 518Z" fill="#f4c771" stroke="#fff0bb" stroke-width="8"/><path d="M222 516Q450 292 679 516" fill="none" stroke="#344f51" stroke-width="14" stroke-dasharray="12 20"/><circle cx="395" cy="391" r="14" fill="#fff5d3"/><path d="M376 449v-44l19-20 19 20v44" fill="#c97260"/><circle cx="529" cy="400" r="14" fill="#fff5d3"/><path d="M510 458v-43l19-19 19 19v43" fill="#b8d4a6"/><g fill="#fbe8ae"><circle cx="280" cy="140" r="4"/><circle cx="365" cy="110" r="3"/><circle cx="584" cy="180" r="4"/><circle cx="627" cy="87" r="3"/></g></svg></div></div></section>
<section class="intro"><h2>Four envelopes.<br>One neighbourhood.</h2><p>You have a pretend $35 and one free hour. Open each envelope and pick a way to help. There is no “best” person to help, and no real money changes hands. The trick is noticing how small, specific help can travel further than it looks.</p></section>
<section class="game" aria-label="Little Bridge interactive game"><div class="dashboard"><h2>Today's little reserves</h2><div class="budget"><div>Cash left<strong id="money">$35</strong></div><div>Time left<strong id="time">60 min</strong></div><div>Bridges made<strong id="count">0 / 4</strong></div></div></div><div class="track" role="progressbar" aria-label="Bridges made" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="4" aria-valuenow="0"><span id="progress"></span></div><div class="game-body"><p class="instruction">Choose one response per envelope. Options you cannot afford are dimmed. Change your mind with “Undo.”</p><div id="cards" class="cards"></div><div id="ending" class="ending" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="footer-row"><button class="reset" id="reset" type="button">↺ Start another round</button><span id="status" class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Every bridge begins with a first step.</span></div></div></section>
<section class="about"><h2>Where this came from</h2><div><p>In 2004 Jon noticed <em>Modest Needs</em>, a project built around helping people with small, unexpected expenses. He wished for a local version in Victoria. This is a little fictional thought experiment in that same spirit, not a fundraising page or advice about real assistance.</p><p>Inspired by Jon's <a href="https://cooltoolsforcatholics.blogspot.com/2004/12/modest-needs.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">“Modest Needs” post ↗</a></p></div></section></main>
<footer>A small bridge is still a bridge. · <a href="./">Back to Chloe Reads Jon</a></footer>
<script>
const cases=[
 {icon:'🚌',tag:'ENVELOPE 01 / GETTING THERE',title:'The interview ride',story:'A neighbour has an interview across town tomorrow. Their bus card ran out tonight.',options:[{label:'Top up a day pass',cash:12,time:0,ripple:'The ride is covered. They arrive with one less thing to worry about.'},{label:'Offer a lift and wait nearby',cash:0,time:25,ripple:'The ride is covered, and there is someone to celebrate with afterward.'}]},
 {icon:'🥣',tag:'ENVELOPE 02 / DINNER',title:'The almost-empty pantry',story:'Payday is Friday; tonight there are three people and not much in the cupboard.',options:[{label:'Leave a grocery bag at the door',cash:18,time:0,ripple:'Dinner is handled, quietly. The family gets to choose what tomorrow looks like.'},{label:'Cook an extra pot and share it',cash:5,time:25,ripple:'A warm meal lands on the table, and you finally exchange recipes.'}]},
 {icon:'💡',tag:'ENVELOPE 03 / HOME',title:'The hallway light',story:'The shared hallway bulb has been out for days. It makes the evening stairs difficult.',options:[{label:'Pick up the right bulb',cash:9,time:0,ripple:'Someone puts it in tonight. The whole floor can see the stairs again.'},{label:'Find a spare and replace it',cash:0,time:20,ripple:'The stairwell is bright by supper, and everyone benefits from a tiny repair.'}]},
 {icon:'✂️',tag:'ENVELOPE 04 / SCHOOL',title:'The model display',story:'Tomorrow is show-and-tell. A child has an idea but not the supplies to finish it.',options:[{label:'Bring a little craft-kit refill',cash:16,time:0,ripple:'The display is ready. The child gets to show the idea they were excited about.'},{label:'Rummage for supplies and build together',cash:0,time:30,ripple:'Cardboard becomes a masterpiece. The story they tell is about making it together.'}]}
];
let choices=Array(4).fill(null);const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);function render(){let usedCash=0,usedTime=0,n=0;choices.forEach((v,i)=>{if(v!==null){usedCash+=cases[i].options[v].cash;usedTime+=cases[i].options[v].time;n++}});const cash=35-usedCash,minutes=60-usedTime;$('money').textContent='$'+cash;$('time').textContent=minutes+' min';$('count').textContent=n+' / 4';$('progress').style.width=(n*25)+'%';document.querySelector('.track').setAttribute('aria-valuenow',String(n));$('cards').replaceChildren();cases.forEach((item,i)=>{const card=document.createElement('article');card.className='card'+(choices[i]!==null?' done':'');const head=document.createElement('div');head.className='card-head';const symbol=document.createElement('div');symbol.className='symbol';symbol.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');symbol.textContent=choices[i]!==null?'✓':item.icon;const words=document.createElement('div');const tag=document.createElement('small');tag.textContent=item.tag;const title=document.createElement('h3');title.textContent=item.title;const story=document.createElement('p');story.textContent=item.story;words.append(tag,title,story);head.append(symbol,words);card.append(head);if(choices[i]===null){const opts=document.createElement('div');opts.className='options';item.options.forEach((opt,j)=>{const b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='option';b.disabled=opt.cash>cash||opt.time>minutes;b.setAttribute('aria-label',opt.label+', '+(opt.cash?'$'+opt.cash:'')+(opt.cash&&opt.time?' and ':'')+(opt.time?opt.time+' minutes':''));const name=document.createElement('span');name.textContent=opt.label;const cost=document.createElement('span');cost.className='cost';cost.textContent=(opt.cash?'$'+opt.cash:'')+(opt.cash&&opt.time?' + ':'')+(opt.time?opt.time+' min':'');b.append(name,cost);b.addEventListener('click',()=>{choices[i]=j;render()});opts.append(b)});card.append(opts)}else{const r=document.createElement('div');r.className='ripple';const lead=document.createElement('b');lead.textContent='BRIDGE MADE';const text=document.createElement('span');text.textContent=item.options[choices[i]].ripple;const undo=document.createElement('button');undo.type='button';undo.textContent='Undo this choice';undo.addEventListener('click',()=>{choices[i]=null;render()});r.append(lead,text,document.createElement('br'),undo);card.append(r)}$('cards').append(card)});const ending=$('ending');ending.classList.toggle('show',n===4);ending.replaceChildren();if(n===4){const h=document.createElement('h3');h.textContent='The block feels a little closer.';const p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent='Four small gaps crossed with $'+usedCash+' and '+usedTime+' minutes. The point was never to solve someone’s whole life. Just to leave a light on for the next step.';const note=document.createElement('p');note.className='end-note';note.textContent='Fictional scenarios. In real life, ask what help is welcome and respect the answer.';ending.append(h,p,note)}$('status').textContent=n===4?'All four bridges made. Beautifully done.':n?'You have made '+n+' of four bridges.':'Every bridge begins with a first step.'}
$('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{choices=Array(4).fill(null);render();$('cards').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'start'})});render();
</script></body></html>
